# Line endings.
#
# .editorconfig sets end_of_line = crlf for the working tree, which suits a Windows
# development machine. This file keeps the repository itself normalised to LF, so a
# checkout on another platform does not produce a diff on every file.
#
# text=auto: Git decides per file whether it is text, normalises it to LF in the index,
# and converts on checkout according to core.autocrlf.
* text=auto

# Files that must stay LF regardless of platform: a CRLF shebang line is a syntax error.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are tool-managed. Leaving them untouched avoids spurious diffs and keeps the
# integrity hashes that some tools compute over the raw bytes.
pnpm-lock.yaml -text
package-lock.json -text

# Binary.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.nupkg binary
*.snupkg binary
